    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. if the failure is localizing due to those stress concentrations and the uneven subgrade support, how do we best differentiate between actual material fatigue and external factors? like, could there be any external physical interference or localized disturbances in the layer that aren't just standard load traffic or thermal stuff?",
